{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired node1’s status writer. It now reloads non-empty configuration on SIGHUP without changing PID, ignores empty configuration, exits cleanly on SIGTERM, runs as exactly one boot-persistent service, and preserves existing journal entries. Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Updated worker.py with Python 2.5-compatible SIGHUP and SIGTERM handlers.","Added a native SysV service for boot persistence and single-instance management.","Tested valid reload, empty-config rejection, clean termination, and journal continuity.","Safely restarted node1 once and verified full recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SIGHUP reloads message.conf without terminating the process or creating a second writer","command_ids":["cmd-a08410e4eac14490","cmd-5e949259b1834cb1"],"summary":"Before and after reboot, the PID remained unchanged, writer count remained exactly one, and subsequent journal entries used the reloaded message."},{"requirement":"Empty configuration is rejected while retaining the last valid message","command_ids":["cmd-fc8d76207e894a7e"],"summary":"With a proven zero-byte message.conf, the same PID continued running as the only writer and appended the prior valid message."},{"requirement":"SIGTERM causes a clean exit","command_ids":["cmd-f1762553800441ea"],"summary":"The sole writer exited with status 0 after SIGTERM, left no writer process, and produced no error output."},{"requirement":"Continue appending the current message and preserve existing journal entries","command_ids":["cmd-fe1a91565e0444d8","cmd-83eb62d140bb4d1a","cmd-dedf978751fc4904","cmd-6edf82fc21a44ad7"],"summary":"The original first entry remains present with the same journal inode, while line-count checks and final tail output prove continued appends before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Remain compatible with the installed legacy OS and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-b58da76d85814d3c","cmd-f1983ed9de9f45ba","cmd-6edf82fc21a44ad7"],"summary":"The repaired source compiled with installed Python 2.5.1; final state remains Ubuntu 7.10 on kernel 2.6.22-14-generic."},{"requirement":"Final service state has exactly one writer and restored production configuration","command_ids":["cmd-6edf82fc21a44ad7","cmd-cd94e33fa1944b47"],"summary":"message.conf is restored to 'branch status: open'; the service is running with one process and only the three intended application files remain."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart sequence","command_ids":["cmd-83eb62d140bb4d1a","cmd-08c9de76cb72440b","cmd-cce611e3325a4296","cmd-5da9e95a91bd4e71","cmd-dedf978751fc4904"],"summary":"Captured healthy baseline boot ID 94c899ff-1d7a-459a-8858-8627f4b28ff7, acknowledged the safe reboot, observed temporary unavailability, then proved boot ID changed to f1ec25b2-2e7a-4f7a-ae7e-576e5cb03e34 and verified automatic service recovery, one writer, preserved data, and continued journal growth."}]}
